version: 33.3.0
date: May 13th, 2025
---

# What's New in AG Grid 33.3

1. Row Pinning
2. Row Height Resizing
3. Grand Total Row Pinning
4. Scroll Column Into View
5. Performance Improvements

Please note that AG Grid 33.3 has no breaking changes from AG Grid 33.x. If you're already using AG Grid 33.x, this upgrade doesn't require any changes to your codebase.

We recommend reviewing the release notes when planning to update to this version.

## Row Pinning

AG Grid 33.3 adds row pinning functionality, allowing end-users to pin rows at the top or bottom of the grid viewport using the context menu or via API. Pinned rows support the full range of features like unpinned rows—they can be selected, sorted, and filtered according to the currently applied column sort and filter conditions.

## Row Height Resizing

This release enables row height resizing by end-users. Users can adjust the row height to suit the data shown in the grid or specific use cases, making the grid row rendering more flexible and adaptable to various scenarios.

## Grand Total Row Pinning

AG Grid 33.3 allows pinning the grand total row, enabling it to be displayed as pinned, either allowing the end-user to unpin it or not, depending on the requirements of your use case.

## Scroll Column Into View

Improvements to the columns tool panel feature allow users to scroll any visible and non-collapsed column into view when not in pivot mode. This enables end-users to easily bring the column they need into view when the grid has a horizontal scrollbar and displays many columns.

## Performance Improvements

AG Grid 33.3 significantly speeds up column generation, especially important when pivoting, as a large number of pivot columns can be generated based on distinct values in the pivoted columns. New column generation is much faster after adding, reordering, or removing pivot and aggregation columns, or changing certain pivot-related grid options.

Additionally, performance improvements have been made in cell flashing after a data update, allowing the grid to support a higher volume of transactions with cell flashing.

These enhancements are part of our ongoing efforts to improve rendering performance and UI responsiveness, enabling users to interact with even larger datasets in the grid.

## Summary

AG Grid 33.3 is an important minor version—it adds key end-user features and improvements in performance and stability. We highly recommend upgrading to this new version to benefit from these enhancements.